\title{bpnmf: Bayesian Panel NMF for Causal Effects on Panel Count Data}
\description{
Estimates causal treatment effects on panel count data (e.g. births, low-birth-weight or preterm outcomes by state and period) via a Bayesian hierarchical model with a low-rank nonnegative factorization of the log-rate surface, fit with Stan through 'cmdstanr'. Supports joint and two-stage cut (modular) inference, censored small-count likelihoods, posterior predictive checks, and publication tables and figures. An R port of the Python package 'bayesian_panel_nmf'.
